class Solution {
    public int myAtoi(String s) {
        int i = 0;
        int n = s.length();
        // Skip leading whitespace
        while (i<n && s.charAt(i)==' '){
            i++;
        }
        if (i == n){
            return 0;
        }
        // Check optional sign
        int sign = 1;
        char firstChar = s.charAt(i);
        if (firstChar == '-'){
            sign = -1;
            i++;
        } else if (firstChar == '+'){
            i++;
        }
        // Parse consecutive digits and guard against 32-bit overflow
        int result = 0;
        while (i < n && Character.isDigit(s.charAt(i))){
            int digit = s.charAt(i) - '0';
            // Clamp to Integer.MAX_VALUE or Integer.MIN_VALUE on overflow
            if (result >(Integer.MAX_VALUE - digit) / 10){
                return (sign == 1) ? Integer.MAX_VALUE : Integer.MIN_VALUE;
            }
            result = result *10 +digit;
            i++;
        }
        return sign*result;
    }
}



/*

Aapko ek string s milegi (jaise "   -42" ya "4193 with words"), aur aapko usmein se valid number nikal kar 32-bit signed integer (-2147483648 se 2147483647 ke beech) return karna hai.

Kaun-Kaun Se Rules Follow Karne Hain?
1. Aage ke spaces hatao: Shuru mein jitne bhi ' ' (spaces) hain, unhe ignore karo.
2. Sign (+ ya -) dekho: Space ke baad agar '-' hai toh number negative hoga, '+' hai toh positive, aur kuch nahi hai toh by default positive maano.
3. Sirf lagatar digits padho: '0' se '9' tak ke characters ko jor kar number banao. Jaise hi koi non-digit character aaye (letter, space, dot, -, etc.), wahin ruk jao.
4. 32-bit limit (overflow) sambhalo: Agar number 2147483647 se bada ho jaye toh 2147483647 return karo, aur -2147483648 se chhota ho jaye toh -2147483648 return karo.

*/



